    "pond": "Dense fine vertical bands disappear in caster-off still and return in both controls. Broad directional response remains.",
    "fountain": "Fine radial bands remain in all three originals. Basin geometry/caster is a hypothesis requiring separate controlled isolation.",
    "river": "All three originals are dominated by transfer-bridge deck; river quality cannot be assessed from them."
  },
  "limits": [
    "Nine water readbacks preserve RGBA hashes and camera position/forward/FOV but not full numeric camera/projection matrices, per-image tick brackets or independent 3D/Canvas marker proofs. Four decoded 3D marker centroids plus three Canvas samples verify the inherited synchronization images only, not each later water camera.",
    "Executed _render_current_frame awaits natural frame_post_draw and asserts no intervening physics/process tick. This is code plus aggregate native assertions; missing per-water metadata has not been reconstructed.",
    "Recorded inventory transforms are Godot strings; resource identities and A/B/A flags are exact native records, not full triangle/topology authentication.",
    "Authored frozen-world views preserve normal default content and isolate personal Music; they are not real-input gameplay, moving-water review or a normal-speed reel. Native shader TIME remains active, so controls are not pixel-identical.",
    "No measured cost, whole-run exclusivity, M5/macOS/AAA acceptance. Root-authorised headless overlap is disclosed in original author analysis; no inference of timing from counter reductions."
  ],
